**SMC means Smart Money Concepts.** It is a way of reading price charts through trends, important price zones, and possible liquidity locations. Traders use these patterns to interpret large participantsâ€™ activity, but a chart pattern cannot prove who traded or whether manipulation occurred. [SMC overview](https://www.luxalgo.com/library/indicator/smart-money-concepts-smc/)

Its main components are:

| Component | Meaning | Application |
|---|---|---|
| **Market structure** | Higher highs/higher lows suggest an uptrend; lower highs/lower lows suggest a downtrend. | Establish market direction. |
| **BOS â€” Break of Structure** | Price breaks a significant swing in the existing trendâ€™s direction. | Identify possible continuation. |
| **CHoCH â€” Change of Character** | Price breaks important structure against the existing trend. | Flag a possible reversal; it needs further confirmation. |
| **Order blocks** | Candidate supply/demand zones associated with a strong move, often marked around an opposing candle before it. | Identify areas to watch for a reaction. |
| **Liquidity and sweeps** | Prior highs/lows are treated as possible stop-order clusters; a sweep moves beyond a level and returns inside. | Investigate failed breakouts and potential targets. |
| **FVG â€” Fair Value Gap** | A three-candle price imbalance where the first and third candlesâ€™ ranges do not overlap. | Mark possible retracement zones; a return is not guaranteed. |
| **Premium/discount** | Priceâ€™s position above/below the midpoint of a selected range. | Judge entry location relative to that range. |

These concepts form a chart-reading framework rather than one fixed strategy. [Structure definitions](https://www.luxalgo.com/library/indicator/smart-money-concepts-smc/), [SMC components](https://fxopen.com/blog/en/the-smart-money-concept-basics-and-strategies/)

A typical approach is: **identify the trend â†’ mark relevant zones â†’ wait for price to reach one â†’ require a defined confirmation â†’ set entry, invalidation, and target.** Its effectiveness must be measured with explicit rules and realistic trading costs.

For **MarketLinkâ€™s first SMC extension**, I recommend starting with:

- Confirmed swing highs/lows and bullish/bearish/ranging state.
- BOS and CHoCH chart labels and alerts.
- Adjustable swing sensitivity and candle-close versus wick-break rules.
- Historical replay that records when each signal actually became available.

Your eight extensions overlapâ€”SMC already includes several liquidity, FVG, and supply/demand ideas. We should share their underlying calculations so the modules remain consistent.

