{"file": "rollout-2026-10-13T01-21-24-01a13190-04da-7773-af76-0aa89a528609.jsonl", "line": 248, "timestamp": "2026-10-13T01:41:20.321Z", "message_id": "msg_0c38f0064b42ade4016acd8c37ddd8819186b8aa55c3a9dd05", "role": "assistant", "phase": "final_answer", "parts": ["<proposed_plan>\n# Clean PDF Reading Guide\n\nCreate **Market-Learning AI â€” Research Plan and Getting Started**, preserving the full roadmap and adding practical guidance for approaching the project.\n\n**This chat is currently in Plan mode, which prevents file creation. No PDF has been generated yet; switch out of Plan mode to produce it.**\n\n## Contents\n\n1. Your vision, confirmed requirements, and realistic research goals.\n2. Beginner explanations of neural learning, experience memory, LLM agents, and backtesting.\n3. The open-source research map, with clickable project and paper links.\n4. A clear architecture diagram and staged development roadmap.\n5. A practical starting sequence: what to read first, what to investigate, and which pilot experiments to run.\n6. Validation gates, common mistakes, and a first-month checklist.\n\n## Presentation\n\nUse A4 pages, readable typography, restrained colors, generous spacing, page numbers, bookmarks, and a linked contents page. Split large comparison tables into readable sections.\n\nClearly distinguish established findings, proposed experiments, and unresolved research questions.\n\n## Verification and delivery\n\nGenerate the PDF, render and visually inspect every page, and check links, bookmarks, tables, and pagination before delivering the download.\n</proposed_plan>"], "text": "<proposed_plan>\n# Clean PDF Reading Guide\n\nCreate **Market-Learning AI â€” Research Plan and Getting Started**, preserving the full roadmap and adding practical guidance for approaching the project.\n\n**This chat is currently in Plan mode, which prevents file creation. No PDF has been generated yet; switch out of Plan mode to produce it.**\n\n## Contents\n\n1. Your vision, confirmed requirements, and realistic research goals.\n2. Beginner explanations of neural learning, experience memory, LLM agents, and backtesting.\n3. The open-source research map, with clickable project and paper links.\n4. A clear architecture diagram and staged development roadmap.\n5. A practical starting sequence: what to read first, what to investigate, and which pilot experiments to run.\n6. Validation gates, common mistakes, and a first-month checklist.\n\n## Presentation\n\nUse A4 pages, readable typography, restrained colors, generous spacing, page numbers, bookmarks, and a linked contents page. Split large comparison tables into readable sections.\n\nClearly distinguish established findings, proposed experiments, and unresolved research questions.\n\n## Verification and delivery\n\nGenerate the PDF, render and visually inspect every page, and check links, bookmarks, tables, and pagination before delivering the download.\n</proposed_plan>", "images": [], "source_kind": "original_assistant_output", "index": 10, "text_sha256": "5f8066c92320ecb2cd20c564d0db8461b6c6368cb0b3d7ac29255308a3513fd5", "section": "conversation"}
