{"file": "rollout-2026-10-13T01-21-24-01a13190-04da-7773-af76-0aa89a528609.jsonl", "line": 1316, "timestamp": "2026-10-13T21:04:03.621Z", "message_id": "msg_0c38f0064b42ade4016ace9cc15ef88191bd59c46c20409043", "role": "assistant", "phase": "commentary", "parts": ["The package describes itself as an early offline foundation and clearly marks the unfinished work. It includes a synthetic replay, reports, tests, and a read-only MT5 adapter; it does not yet include broker tick export, model training, or AI agents. Iâ€™m checking whether its tests and packaged evidence support those claims.\n"], "text": "The package describes itself as an early offline foundation and clearly marks the unfinished work. It includes a synthetic replay, reports, tests, and a read-only MT5 adapter; it does not yet include broker tick export, model training, or AI agents. Iâ€™m checking whether its tests and packaged evidence support those claims.\n", "images": [], "source_kind": "visible_chat_event", "index": 33, "text_sha256": "e49eedf32437209003a010b4a78a91ff3c9a54803c8848aa0a68089297af6a86", "section": "conversation"}
{"file": "rollout-2026-10-13T01-21-24-01a13190-04da-7773-af76-0aa89a528609.jsonl", "line": 1423, "timestamp": "2026-10-13T21:10:15.998Z", "message_id": "msg_0c38f0064b42ade4016ace9e351d1081918c28a9e11143b62f", "role": "assistant", "phase": "commentary", "parts": ["I reproduced the fixture results and checked the shipped file hashes. On Windows with its pinned Python 3.13 dependencies, the suite ran 115 tests: 112 passed, one failed, and two were skipped. Separate probes found bugs in reversal margin checks, receipt-time validation, tick interval filtering, and malformed-report handling that the existing tests missed.\n"], "text": "I reproduced the fixture results and checked the shipped file hashes. On Windows with its pinned Python 3.13 dependencies, the suite ran 115 tests: 112 passed, one failed, and two were skipped. Separate probes found bugs in reversal margin checks, receipt-time validation, tick interval filtering, and malformed-report handling that the existing tests missed.\n", "images": [], "source_kind": "visible_chat_event", "index": 34, "text_sha256": "7d301e6ebb2ad0c837305e968f7368667d53e418fdf6aa9e062071ab5714296b", "section": "conversation"}
{"file": "rollout-2026-10-13T01-21-24-01a13190-04da-7773-af76-0aa89a528609.jsonl", "line": 1488, "timestamp": "2026-10-13T21:16:15.598Z", "message_id": "msg_0c38f0064b42ade4016ace9f965e9881918884ab843887292b", "role": "assistant", "phase": "final_answer", "parts": ["Checked it. **Itâ€™s a useful offline starter, but four correctness issues need fixing:**\n\n- **Margin checks:** reversing a position can open new exposure without enough margin.\n- **Data timing:** receipt-based records can expose information before it actually arrived, allowing future-data leakage.\n- **Report handling:** one malformed manifest can crash the entire review index.\n- **MT5 intervals:** fractional-millisecond boundaries can select the wrong ticks.\n\nI reproduced these with offline probes.\n\nOn Windows with its pinned Python 3.13 dependencies, **112 tests passed, 1 failed, and 2 were skipped**. The failure concerns Windows path normalization. The default synthetic results and checkpoint recovery reproduced correctly.\n\n**It does not yet learn strategies or backtest your actual Exness history.** Tick export, storage, model training, agents, and memory remain unfinishedâ€”and the documentation honestly acknowledges that.\n\n[Full review, evidence, and recommended fixes](<C:/Users/EHOSANUR RAHMAN ROMI/Desktop/codex/reviews/market-learning-starter-20261014-e41d09f/REVIEW.md>)\n\nYour ZIP was preserved; I made no source fixes or MT5 connections.\n\n"], "text": "Checked it. **Itâ€™s a useful offline starter, but four correctness issues need fixing:**\n\n- **Margin checks:** reversing a position can open new exposure without enough margin.\n- **Data timing:** receipt-based records can expose information before it actually arrived, allowing future-data leakage.\n- **Report handling:** one malformed manifest can crash the entire review index.\n- **MT5 intervals:** fractional-millisecond boundaries can select the wrong ticks.\n\nI reproduced these with offline probes.\n\nOn Windows with its pinned Python 3.13 dependencies, **112 tests passed, 1 failed, and 2 were skipped**. The failure concerns Windows path normalization. The default synthetic results and checkpoint recovery reproduced correctly.\n\n**It does not yet learn strategies or backtest your actual Exness history.** Tick export, storage, model training, agents, and memory remain unfinishedâ€”and the documentation honestly acknowledges that.\n\n[Full review, evidence, and recommended fixes](<C:/Users/EHOSANUR RAHMAN ROMI/Desktop/codex/reviews/market-learning-starter-20261014-e41d09f/REVIEW.md>)\n\nYour ZIP was preserved; I made no source fixes or MT5 connections.\n\n", "images": [], "source_kind": "visible_chat_event", "index": 35, "text_sha256": "e7a911debec7058874ed8b4ef9839c5fed28a8ab867519b6f58c60dc86529d01", "section": "conversation"}
