{"file": "rollout-2026-10-15T13-43-10-01a13e83-da25-79c2-8413-bcf2766efa8a.jsonl", "line": 4608, "timestamp": "2026-10-15T17:38:50.842Z", "message_id": "msg_0c38f0064b42ade4016ad10fa8c258819197ee090421e49248", "role": "assistant", "phase": "commentary", "parts": ["The trend experiment found a better development result: PF 1.37 across 118 trades, with positive results in all three development folds. It still falls short of PF 2 and has no real-tick validation. The audit also found a signal-state bug that can skip later breakouts; Iâ€™m correcting it and recording a separate rerun so the original results remain visible.\n"], "text": "The trend experiment found a better development result: PF 1.37 across 118 trades, with positive results in all three development folds. It still falls short of PF 2 and has no real-tick validation. The audit also found a signal-state bug that can skip later breakouts; Iâ€™m correcting it and recording a separate rerun so the original results remain visible.\n", "images": [], "source_kind": "visible_chat_event", "index": 141, "text_sha256": "eb253adbf7fe9207186d9e6b1b8df38d27de390ebd7e207d6860f198dfb885f2", "section": "conversation"}
{"file": "rollout-2026-10-15T13-43-10-01a13e83-da25-79c2-8413-bcf2766efa8a.jsonl", "line": 4698, "timestamp": "2026-10-15T17:43:43.275Z", "message_id": "msg_0c38f0064b42ade4016ad110cce75481919e0e14c27e4f0e5d", "role": "assistant", "phase": "commentary", "parts": ["The trade-count check found concrete limits: sweep setups produced 51 trades, impulse/correction 51, and ADX pullbacks 60. Many pending entries were invalidated or rejected because costs were too large relative to the stop. Iâ€™m keeping those rejection reasons visible in the new research workspace, alongside the variables, charts and trade ledger.\n"], "text": "The trade-count check found concrete limits: sweep setups produced 51 trades, impulse/correction 51, and ADX pullbacks 60. Many pending entries were invalidated or rejected because costs were too large relative to the stop. Iâ€™m keeping those rejection reasons visible in the new research workspace, alongside the variables, charts and trade ledger.\n", "images": [], "source_kind": "visible_chat_event", "index": 142, "text_sha256": "33c00ec4b39b8c65d4959d8e8347dd9f518dbfc2ce08a14fc5fa460d586448fb", "section": "conversation"}
{"file": "rollout-2026-10-15T13-43-10-01a13e83-da25-79c2-8413-bcf2766efa8a.jsonl", "line": 4760, "timestamp": "2026-10-15T17:46:34.727Z", "message_id": "msg_0c38f0064b42ade4016ad11177a078819192bc70315e7067c8", "role": "assistant", "phase": "commentary", "parts": ["The corrected trend run reached PF 1.40 across 118 development trades; none of the 1,632 recorded screens met PF 2. The cost maths also explains some rejected setups: our declared spread, commission and slippage total about $0.434 per ounce, so the 20% cost limit requires a stop distance of at least $2.17. Wider stops change trade outcomes too, so they must be tested rather than treated as a shortcut to profit.\n"], "text": "The corrected trend run reached PF 1.40 across 118 development trades; none of the 1,632 recorded screens met PF 2. The cost maths also explains some rejected setups: our declared spread, commission and slippage total about $0.434 per ounce, so the 20% cost limit requires a stop distance of at least $2.17. Wider stops change trade outcomes too, so they must be tested rather than treated as a shortcut to profit.\n", "images": [], "source_kind": "visible_chat_event", "index": 143, "text_sha256": "3600d12eeb69a47a1525053a0ebc591775f9b5a708097f247dcf0e9dd6d8a576", "section": "conversation"}
