{"file": "rollout-2026-10-15T13-43-10-01a13e83-da25-79c2-8413-bcf2766efa8a.jsonl", "line": 9130, "timestamp": "2026-10-15T22:30:19.321Z", "message_id": "msg_0c38f0064b42ade4016ad153f9f9a48191aff9f5b73115b6ab", "role": "assistant", "phase": "commentary", "parts": ["Gold March reached the declared 300-second timeout. Its cancellation receipt is retained, and MT5 is idle again.\n\nThe full Aprilâ€“October development period is available, so Iâ€™ll evaluate from April as planned. I also closed two storage-check gaps: source snapshot copies and ledger appends now check their size before writing. The runner passes 66 synthetic checks.\n"], "text": "Gold March reached the declared 300-second timeout. Its cancellation receipt is retained, and MT5 is idle again.\n\nThe full Aprilâ€“October development period is available, so Iâ€™ll evaluate from April as planned. I also closed two storage-check gaps: source snapshot copies and ledger appends now check their size before writing. The runner passes 66 synthetic checks.\n", "images": [], "source_kind": "visible_chat_event", "index": 207, "text_sha256": "c9389c3ae3a8a0f4086ba1b242342e6deb062f20efaba38bcc0ba8bfbea6ed7b", "section": "conversation"}
{"file": "rollout-2026-10-15T13-43-10-01a13e83-da25-79c2-8413-bcf2766efa8a.jsonl", "line": 9165, "timestamp": "2026-10-15T22:32:21.776Z", "message_id": "msg_0c38f0064b42ade4016ad1547488188191a526ce4c75d2996b", "role": "assistant", "phase": "commentary", "parts": ["The Aprilâ€“October evaluation has started using **57.1 million original Gold and Silver quote records**. It is checking source hashes, minute coverage and recorded spreads before calculating any strategy performance.\n\nAbout **42.5 GiB remains free**. The 188 focused synthetic checks passed, and Iâ€™ve added the cohortâ€™s checks to the normal build process.\n"], "text": "The Aprilâ€“October evaluation has started using **57.1 million original Gold and Silver quote records**. It is checking source hashes, minute coverage and recorded spreads before calculating any strategy performance.\n\nAbout **42.5 GiB remains free**. The 188 focused synthetic checks passed, and Iâ€™ve added the cohortâ€™s checks to the normal build process.\n", "images": [], "source_kind": "visible_chat_event", "index": 208, "text_sha256": "d19a66c6ca44a1a0346eab7c9e19b8e045ad9268ad1d5bb550d102fba2aa958d", "section": "conversation"}
{"file": "rollout-2026-10-15T13-43-10-01a13e83-da25-79c2-8413-bcf2766efa8a.jsonl", "line": 9211, "timestamp": "2026-10-15T22:34:40.542Z", "message_id": "msg_0c38f0064b42ade4016ad154fe53b88191b1562e01689aaab5", "role": "assistant", "phase": "commentary", "parts": ["The first paired-market cohort stopped before trading simulation: only **1 of 140 completed sessions** met the fixed quote-freshness requirement, so it never obtained the required 20 prior valid sessions.\n\nThat leaves PF unknownâ€”no performance was calculated. Iâ€™m preserving this result and reviewing the observation method as a separate experiment. The completed cohortâ€™s rules will stay fixed.\n"], "text": "The first paired-market cohort stopped before trading simulation: only **1 of 140 completed sessions** met the fixed quote-freshness requirement, so it never obtained the required 20 prior valid sessions.\n\nThat leaves PF unknownâ€”no performance was calculated. Iâ€™m preserving this result and reviewing the observation method as a separate experiment. The completed cohortâ€™s rules will stay fixed.\n", "images": [], "source_kind": "visible_chat_event", "index": 209, "text_sha256": "3a75d464b9583980fbf0f4f27c2763cc853f1b11de6dc28bfd358a170aeabad0", "section": "conversation"}
{"file": "rollout-2026-10-15T13-43-10-01a13e83-da25-79c2-8413-bcf2766efa8a.jsonl", "line": 9313, "timestamp": "2026-10-15T22:40:11.187Z", "message_id": "msg_0c38f0064b42ade4016ad15649a628819192155a0a19bb76cd", "role": "assistant", "phase": "commentary", "parts": ["Iâ€™ve published the stopped cohortâ€™s results and the next experiment design to your private repository.\n\nIâ€™m now separating training observations from entry decisions: the new experiment will test a five-second training tolerance while keeping strict one-second crossing observations. It is a separate protocol, with the original cohort preserved. Disk space remains at **42.52 GiB free**.\n"], "text": "Iâ€™ve published the stopped cohortâ€™s results and the next experiment design to your private repository.\n\nIâ€™m now separating training observations from entry decisions: the new experiment will test a five-second training tolerance while keeping strict one-second crossing observations. It is a separate protocol, with the original cohort preserved. Disk space remains at **42.52 GiB free**.\n", "images": [], "source_kind": "visible_chat_event", "index": 210, "text_sha256": "2e104cc0be36d4770d41d71450543fb78ac728cc60ba2c040d1641e556d800fe", "section": "conversation"}
{"file": "rollout-2026-10-15T13-43-10-01a13e83-da25-79c2-8413-bcf2766efa8a.jsonl", "line": 9384, "timestamp": "2026-10-15T22:44:37.039Z", "message_id": "msg_0c38f0064b42ade4016ad157547040819197a4b7a4e59e228c", "role": "assistant", "phase": "commentary", "parts": ["Iâ€™m continuing the new observation experiment, first checking which edits survived the interruption. Iâ€™ll keep the first cohortâ€™s result intact and monitor disk space before running the revised protocol.\n"], "text": "Iâ€™m continuing the new observation experiment, first checking which edits survived the interruption. Iâ€™ll keep the first cohortâ€™s result intact and monitor disk space before running the revised protocol.\n", "images": [], "source_kind": "visible_chat_event", "index": 211, "text_sha256": "7d2c0db19a98c2cb1a1131769362f38f9c00394b3097d75a1fac2a6015b4181f", "section": "conversation"}
{"file": "rollout-2026-10-15T13-43-10-01a13e83-da25-79c2-8413-bcf2766efa8a.jsonl", "line": 9473, "timestamp": "2026-10-15T22:47:14.660Z", "message_id": "msg_0c38f0064b42ade4016ad157f163988191b577bdf13916b698", "role": "assistant", "phase": "commentary", "parts": ["The revised replay keeps training and trading separate: a five-second-old state may inform historical statistics, but it cannot trigger an entry, rearm a trade or trigger a ratio exit. Cash stops and emergency exits remain active.\n\nThe replay has passed all 37 existing tests plus 11 new tests. Iâ€™m finishing the coverage diagnostics and source checks before the next data run.\n"], "text": "The revised replay keeps training and trading separate: a five-second-old state may inform historical statistics, but it cannot trigger an entry, rearm a trade or trigger a ratio exit. Cash stops and emergency exits remain active.\n\nThe replay has passed all 37 existing tests plus 11 new tests. Iâ€™m finishing the coverage diagnostics and source checks before the next data run.\n", "images": [], "source_kind": "visible_chat_event", "index": 212, "text_sha256": "84fac1ab0804b96ce8a83bc0bf77701f74d96b1bc013a0a447d82aa92dd1fbd0", "section": "conversation"}
{"file": "rollout-2026-10-15T13-43-10-01a13e83-da25-79c2-8413-bcf2766efa8a.jsonl", "line": 9593, "timestamp": "2026-10-15T22:50:25.117Z", "message_id": "msg_0c38f0064b42ade4016ad158afac0c8191b43e7b43e344577c", "role": "assistant", "phase": "commentary", "parts": ["The second cohort is running with the revised observation policy and the same frozen Aprilâ€“October data. It retains the three strategy settings, risk limits, costs, delays and pass/fail requirements.\n\nThe current core, extractor, replay and runner suites passed **306 synthetic checks**. The run will first report coverage; if prior-session context is available, it will execute all nine declared controls.\n"], "text": "The second cohort is running with the revised observation policy and the same frozen Aprilâ€“October data. It retains the three strategy settings, risk limits, costs, delays and pass/fail requirements.\n\nThe current core, extractor, replay and runner suites passed **306 synthetic checks**. The run will first report coverage; if prior-session context is available, it will execute all nine declared controls.\n", "images": [], "source_kind": "visible_chat_event", "index": 213, "text_sha256": "c4664d05ec70c09af4c21f71b9194e63cb3ac6b2440b8ecee00fe3f932339ed0", "section": "conversation"}
{"file": "rollout-2026-10-15T13-43-10-01a13e83-da25-79c2-8413-bcf2766efa8a.jsonl", "line": 9645, "timestamp": "2026-10-15T22:52:03.582Z", "message_id": "01a141c3-f460-7e10-9cab-8038430927ed", "role": "user", "phase": null, "parts": ["i need a self learn engine, that can learm from its mistake, and improve the tradings, you can search on git hub for related projects and add to smc core\n"], "text": "i need a self learn engine, that can learm from its mistake, and improve the tradings, you can search on git hub for related projects and add to smc core\n", "images": [], "source_kind": "visible_chat_event", "index": 214, "text_sha256": "ec0dddc5a493207be7f5bac2ee0352d7c19b46c9da2d7fed0548431ac17d4b86", "section": "conversation"}
{"file": "rollout-2026-10-15T13-43-10-01a13e83-da25-79c2-8413-bcf2766efa8a.jsonl", "line": 9648, "timestamp": "2026-10-15T22:52:09.496Z", "message_id": "msg_0c38f0064b42ade4016ad159180b8081918e289f76e0576306", "role": "assistant", "phase": "commentary", "parts": ["Iâ€™ll add a learning layer around the SMC core that records trade outcomes, identifies recurring failure conditions and proposes changes for fresh testing. Proposed changes will need to pass validation before promotion.\n\nIâ€™ll research relevant GitHub projects and inspect the appâ€™s current learning code. The running Gold/Silver experiment will continue separately, with its results preserved.\n"], "text": "Iâ€™ll add a learning layer around the SMC core that records trade outcomes, identifies recurring failure conditions and proposes changes for fresh testing. Proposed changes will need to pass validation before promotion.\n\nIâ€™ll research relevant GitHub projects and inspect the appâ€™s current learning code. The running Gold/Silver experiment will continue separately, with its results preserved.\n", "images": [], "source_kind": "visible_chat_event", "index": 215, "text_sha256": "12a2f1e7e675008aafb76dcd2b3cf0e722dc205ac4bf601262beee48414d313a", "section": "conversation"}
{"file": "rollout-2026-10-15T13-43-10-01a13e83-da25-79c2-8413-bcf2766efa8a.jsonl", "line": 9724, "timestamp": "2026-10-15T22:54:31.904Z", "message_id": "msg_0c38f0064b42ade4016ad159a61a8c81919de791c4a24c66fb", "role": "assistant", "phase": "commentary", "parts": ["The GitHub research supports a practical approach: predict first, wait for the trade to close, then update the model using the cost-aware outcome. River and Qlib provide useful patterns for that workflow.\n\nThe SMC library I reviewed also uses future candles in some batch calculations. Iâ€™ll keep MarketLinkâ€™s existing confirmation-time rules so the learner cannot use information that arrived after its decision.\n"], "text": "The GitHub research supports a practical approach: predict first, wait for the trade to close, then update the model using the cost-aware outcome. River and Qlib provide useful patterns for that workflow.\n\nThe SMC library I reviewed also uses future candles in some batch calculations. Iâ€™ll keep MarketLinkâ€™s existing confirmation-time rules so the learner cannot use information that arrived after its decision.\n", "images": [], "source_kind": "visible_chat_event", "index": 216, "text_sha256": "618b5d90185a0e64413aeb4450b426d319d66d5f30fcbbc6b7044a752c3f5920", "section": "conversation"}
{"file": "rollout-2026-10-15T13-43-10-01a13e83-da25-79c2-8413-bcf2766efa8a.jsonl", "line": 9766, "timestamp": "2026-10-15T22:55:57.227Z", "message_id": "msg_0c38f0064b42ade4016ad159fb934c8191a8215401850040d8", "role": "assistant", "phase": "commentary", "parts": ["The learning engine will keep a record of each prediction, the model version used, when the tradeâ€™s outcome became available, and what changed after learning from it. Its report will separate ordinary losses from poor predictions.\n\nIt will use completed simulated tradesâ€”including shadow labels for skipped baseline tradesâ€”rather than inventing outcomes for trades skipped in live markets. A learned challenger will still need a fresh tick replay and the existing validation gates.\n"], "text": "The learning engine will keep a record of each prediction, the model version used, when the tradeâ€™s outcome became available, and what changed after learning from it. Its report will separate ordinary losses from poor predictions.\n\nIt will use completed simulated tradesâ€”including shadow labels for skipped baseline tradesâ€”rather than inventing outcomes for trades skipped in live markets. A learned challenger will still need a fresh tick replay and the existing validation gates.\n", "images": [], "source_kind": "visible_chat_event", "index": 217, "text_sha256": "3dd44c811127561223ebf843475efe1ada02f095ee67c37cbaf678b2c94814a2", "section": "conversation"}
{"file": "rollout-2026-10-15T13-43-10-01a13e83-da25-79c2-8413-bcf2766efa8a.jsonl", "line": 9955, "timestamp": "2026-10-15T23:02:10.840Z", "message_id": "msg_0c38f0064b42ade4016ad15b7157608191b63b01251884e89b", "role": "assistant", "phase": "commentary", "parts": ["The paired-market run finished with zero trades: all nine controls rejected every signal because the minimum lots could not fit both the risk budget and hedge-balance limit. That failure is preserved.\n\nFor the SMC learner, review caught an important timing issue: the signal decision happens before the fill. Iâ€™m capturing both timestamps so new records learn only from information available at the decision. Older records will be clearly labelled as post-fill shadow analysis.\n"], "text": "The paired-market run finished with zero trades: all nine controls rejected every signal because the minimum lots could not fit both the risk budget and hedge-balance limit. That failure is preserved.\n\nFor the SMC learner, review caught an important timing issue: the signal decision happens before the fill. Iâ€™m capturing both timestamps so new records learn only from information available at the decision. Older records will be clearly labelled as post-fill shadow analysis.\n", "images": [], "source_kind": "visible_chat_event", "index": 218, "text_sha256": "a0aa84a0bf7b954f275d14fce8345771435dae80f7374a3980a9e09a174cd942", "section": "conversation"}
{"file": "rollout-2026-10-15T13-43-10-01a13e83-da25-79c2-8413-bcf2766efa8a.jsonl", "line": 10064, "timestamp": "2026-10-15T23:07:18.739Z", "message_id": "msg_0c38f0064b42ade4016ad15ca5e50c8191924213b8aecc2996", "role": "assistant", "phase": "commentary", "parts": ["Iâ€™m continuing the SMC learning integration. The learner and decision-timing checks are implemented; Iâ€™m fixing saved-report loading, then Iâ€™ll run an offline pilot and package the Windows build.\n"], "text": "Iâ€™m continuing the SMC learning integration. The learner and decision-timing checks are implemented; Iâ€™m fixing saved-report loading, then Iâ€™ll run an offline pilot and package the Windows build.\n", "images": [], "source_kind": "visible_chat_event", "index": 219, "text_sha256": "6d5d0adf63dc7140727dd5d3943468b82e4559f84ef8a39ce7fcc58a33f716b2", "section": "conversation"}
{"file": "rollout-2026-10-15T13-43-10-01a13e83-da25-79c2-8413-bcf2766efa8a.jsonl", "line": 10111, "timestamp": "2026-10-15T23:09:15.600Z", "message_id": "msg_0c38f0064b42ade4016ad15d192e608191917bac43a3142e00", "role": "assistant", "phase": "commentary", "parts": ["Iâ€™m adding a second replay pass that applies the learnerâ€™s take/skip decisions and recalculates fills, lot sizes, equity and missed signals. That will let us compare an executable simulation with the original SMC baseline, rather than relying only on a filtered trade ledger.\n\nThis remains research-only; the active trading runner will stay unchanged.\n"], "text": "Iâ€™m adding a second replay pass that applies the learnerâ€™s take/skip decisions and recalculates fills, lot sizes, equity and missed signals. That will let us compare an executable simulation with the original SMC baseline, rather than relying only on a filtered trade ledger.\n\nThis remains research-only; the active trading runner will stay unchanged.\n", "images": [], "source_kind": "visible_chat_event", "index": 220, "text_sha256": "6926e760c11a998904292677c1e32fb3df885a2b0c34dde665b1dcd73ccc352d", "section": "conversation"}
{"file": "rollout-2026-10-15T13-43-10-01a13e83-da25-79c2-8413-bcf2766efa8a.jsonl", "line": 10254, "timestamp": "2026-10-15T23:16:33.594Z", "message_id": "msg_0c38f0064b42ade4016ad15ecf9074819191e80927f18623e9", "role": "assistant", "phase": "commentary", "parts": ["The learning engine, mistake memory, and separate replay of its take/skip decisions are implemented. The new tests pass. One existing cancellation test failed during the full build; Iâ€™m checking that before packaging, then Iâ€™ll measure the learner on the fixed 2026 Exness data.\n"], "text": "The learning engine, mistake memory, and separate replay of its take/skip decisions are implemented. The new tests pass. One existing cancellation test failed during the full build; Iâ€™m checking that before packaging, then Iâ€™ll measure the learner on the fixed 2026 Exness data.\n", "images": [], "source_kind": "visible_chat_event", "index": 221, "text_sha256": "70736c08f6834e924fe8e622095a2a608aa43007b0d233577e3f111d777a831a", "section": "conversation"}
{"file": "rollout-2026-10-15T13-43-10-01a13e83-da25-79c2-8413-bcf2766efa8a.jsonl", "line": 10326, "timestamp": "2026-10-15T23:18:24.787Z", "message_id": "msg_0c38f0064b42ade4016ad15f3f88548191b06bf2c875d6a406", "role": "assistant", "phase": "commentary", "parts": ["The new model learns from closed simulated trade outcomes, records its prediction mistakes, and adjusts later take/skip decisions. I also found and am fixing a data consistency issue: its chart features must use the same valid Bid/Ask quotes as the simulator.\n"], "text": "The new model learns from closed simulated trade outcomes, records its prediction mistakes, and adjusts later take/skip decisions. I also found and am fixing a data consistency issue: its chart features must use the same valid Bid/Ask quotes as the simulator.\n", "images": [], "source_kind": "visible_chat_event", "index": 222, "text_sha256": "a6d4719fcdf4f09a0183fd917d013d1c07b513d4871648a7e523cdd3c93b5f7c", "section": "conversation"}
{"file": "rollout-2026-10-15T13-43-10-01a13e83-da25-79c2-8413-bcf2766efa8a.jsonl", "line": 10409, "timestamp": "2026-10-15T23:20:28.176Z", "message_id": "msg_0c38f0064b42ade4016ad15fbab53481919d10201202065022", "role": "assistant", "phase": "commentary", "parts": ["The consistency fix passes its regression test, and the remaining build checks pass. Iâ€™m now running the frozen learning policy on the retained 2026 data. The original-tick pilot will compare two separate simulated accounts, recalculating costs and lot sizes after skipped entries.\n"], "text": "The consistency fix passes its regression test, and the remaining build checks pass. Iâ€™m now running the frozen learning policy on the retained 2026 data. The original-tick pilot will compare two separate simulated accounts, recalculating costs and lot sizes after skipped entries.\n", "images": [], "source_kind": "visible_chat_event", "index": 223, "text_sha256": "82b67678b7d1229c820c91cc820dd8e52219235debb3f96925fd39a4d2b14786", "section": "conversation"}
{"file": "rollout-2026-10-15T13-43-10-01a13e83-da25-79c2-8413-bcf2766efa8a.jsonl", "line": 10449, "timestamp": "2026-10-15T23:21:59.750Z", "message_id": "msg_0c38f0064b42ade4016ad160156890819191416902a9c12cb6", "role": "assistant", "phase": "commentary", "parts": ["The original-tick pilot completed: 3.67 million quotes, 100 learning updates, and 50 skipped predictions. It did **not** improve profitability: baseline PF was 1.1121; the learning replay was 1.1113. Drawdown fell, but it also skipped profitable trades. Iâ€™m preserving this failed trial and its mistake records in the app.\n"], "text": "The original-tick pilot completed: 3.67 million quotes, 100 learning updates, and 50 skipped predictions. It did **not** improve profitability: baseline PF was 1.1121; the learning replay was 1.1113. Drawdown fell, but it also skipped profitable trades. Iâ€™m preserving this failed trial and its mistake records in the app.\n", "images": [], "source_kind": "visible_chat_event", "index": 224, "text_sha256": "6dee13eb97c769bcd627688205315a41faf490ef16e58555018c89d0a2ec8ce3", "section": "conversation"}
{"file": "rollout-2026-10-15T13-43-10-01a13e83-da25-79c2-8413-bcf2766efa8a.jsonl", "line": 10515, "timestamp": "2026-10-15T23:25:08.558Z", "message_id": "msg_0c38f0064b42ade4016ad160d2de048191818f9982d9a2f41e", "role": "assistant", "phase": "commentary", "parts": ["The replay confirmed that the model updated its weights, but the first policy mostly learned to skip trades after warmup. Its saved report records that limitation and the skipped winners. Iâ€™m finishing the Windows package and checking that the new screens display this evidence accurately.\n"], "text": "The replay confirmed that the model updated its weights, but the first policy mostly learned to skip trades after warmup. Its saved report records that limitation and the skipped winners. Iâ€™m finishing the Windows package and checking that the new screens display this evidence accurately.\n", "images": [], "source_kind": "visible_chat_event", "index": 225, "text_sha256": "f55fc246cad5924a3459413fb8ce86bc9be9f6a1bdf341dd53edb3cea4fc374e", "section": "conversation"}
{"file": "rollout-2026-10-15T13-43-10-01a13e83-da25-79c2-8413-bcf2766efa8a.jsonl", "line": 10616, "timestamp": "2026-10-15T23:28:21.926Z", "message_id": "msg_0c38f0064b42ade4016ad1619494f48191a9785261b9391934", "role": "assistant", "phase": "commentary", "parts": ["The independent audit matched every prediction, learning update, gate decision, and trade-ledger total. The installer and portable archive are built, with their contents verified by hash. Iâ€™m completing the final screen checks before publishing them to your private GitHub repository.\n"], "text": "The independent audit matched every prediction, learning update, gate decision, and trade-ledger total. The installer and portable archive are built, with their contents verified by hash. Iâ€™m completing the final screen checks before publishing them to your private GitHub repository.\n", "images": [], "source_kind": "visible_chat_event", "index": 226, "text_sha256": "995261e99ada83ab19c86cc2867e9a5212cdf1287156db846c77584f098e0739", "section": "conversation"}
{"file": "rollout-2026-10-15T13-43-10-01a13e83-da25-79c2-8413-bcf2766efa8a.jsonl", "line": 10691, "timestamp": "2026-10-15T23:31:16.297Z", "message_id": "msg_0c38f0064b42ade4016ad1623e9ae08191b5782b1ac0a690ee", "role": "assistant", "phase": "final_answer", "parts": ["Implemented the first self-learning research engine in **MarketLink 3.4**. It learns from closed simulated trades, updates weights, records mistakes, and replays its take/skip decisions separately.\n\n[Download Windows installer](<C:/Users/EHOSANUR RAHMAN ROMI/Downloads/MarketLink-3.4.0-Setup.exe>) Â· [Private GitHub release](https://github.com/EhosanurRahmanRomi/marketlink-mt5-bridge/releases/tag/v3.4.0)\n\nClose the existing MarketLink before installing. Then open **Local AI â†’ Self-learning engine**.\n\n**Verification:** 866 implementation checks and 46 pilot checks passed; all six new screens were visually inspected.\n\n**Actual result:** on 3.67 million 2026 quotes, PF changed from **1.1121 to 1.1113**. The model learned, but profitability did not improve. Fees/slippage remain assumptions; live adaptation is disabled.\n\n[Research sources and usage guide](<C:/Users/EHOSANUR RAHMAN ROMI/Desktop/codex/mt5-desktop-bridge/docs/SMC-SELF-LEARNING.md>)\n\n"], "text": "Implemented the first self-learning research engine in **MarketLink 3.4**. It learns from closed simulated trades, updates weights, records mistakes, and replays its take/skip decisions separately.\n\n[Download Windows installer](<C:/Users/EHOSANUR RAHMAN ROMI/Downloads/MarketLink-3.4.0-Setup.exe>) Â· [Private GitHub release](https://github.com/EhosanurRahmanRomi/marketlink-mt5-bridge/releases/tag/v3.4.0)\n\nClose the existing MarketLink before installing. Then open **Local AI â†’ Self-learning engine**.\n\n**Verification:** 866 implementation checks and 46 pilot checks passed; all six new screens were visually inspected.\n\n**Actual result:** on 3.67 million 2026 quotes, PF changed from **1.1121 to 1.1113**. The model learned, but profitability did not improve. Fees/slippage remain assumptions; live adaptation is disabled.\n\n[Research sources and usage guide](<C:/Users/EHOSANUR RAHMAN ROMI/Desktop/codex/mt5-desktop-bridge/docs/SMC-SELF-LEARNING.md>)\n\n", "images": [], "source_kind": "visible_chat_event", "index": 227, "text_sha256": "1a004aa25232dc0fd97d293058afb66a757e984606cee9fc0012c8db0add660f", "section": "conversation"}
{"file": "rollout-2026-10-15T13-43-10-01a13e83-da25-79c2-8413-bcf2766efa8a.jsonl", "line": 10700, "timestamp": "2026-10-15T23:58:20.282Z", "message_id": "msg_0c38f0064b42ade4016ad1689ab5908191b04663e9be4e2477", "role": "assistant", "phase": "commentary", "parts": ["The last turn made concrete progress: the learning engine was built and audited, and its first tick replay showed that the probability-only filter did not improve returns. Iâ€™ll use that failure to guide the next hypothesis, while checking the remaining untouched data and execution-cost evidence before another test.\n"], "text": "The last turn made concrete progress: the learning engine was built and audited, and its first tick replay showed that the probability-only filter did not improve returns. Iâ€™ll use that failure to guide the next hypothesis, while checking the remaining untouched data and execution-cost evidence before another test.\n", "images": [], "source_kind": "visible_chat_event", "index": 228, "text_sha256": "83646eb7dbc294f00520774b771ee06dfff66369048baa6d3aa14ab2b03a66a1", "section": "conversation"}
{"file": "rollout-2026-10-15T13-43-10-01a13e83-da25-79c2-8413-bcf2766efa8a.jsonl", "line": 10752, "timestamp": "2026-10-16T00:01:44.924Z", "message_id": "msg_0c38f0064b42ade4016ad1696741b881918d0f3ccd392fc289", "role": "assistant", "phase": "commentary", "parts": ["The exposure audit shows that Goldâ€™s earlier validation periods have already been used; I canâ€™t honestly reuse them as fresh proof. The next policy will estimate net payoff, including loss size and configured costs, instead of only win probability. Iâ€™ll test it on exposed development data first and reserve any independent evaluation for a frozen candidate.\n"], "text": "The exposure audit shows that Goldâ€™s earlier validation periods have already been used; I canâ€™t honestly reuse them as fresh proof. The next policy will estimate net payoff, including loss size and configured costs, instead of only win probability. Iâ€™ll test it on exposed development data first and reserve any independent evaluation for a frozen candidate.\n", "images": [], "source_kind": "visible_chat_event", "index": 229, "text_sha256": "328317041d31332f72bc38bffdb87caf971af5528dec40e1b89d7525bd5bc05c", "section": "conversation"}
{"file": "rollout-2026-10-15T13-43-10-01a13e83-da25-79c2-8413-bcf2766efa8a.jsonl", "line": 10771, "timestamp": "2026-10-16T00:04:02.797Z", "message_id": "msg_0c38f0064b42ade4016ad169f1181c81919404d44dd43bb3a8", "role": "assistant", "phase": "commentary", "parts": ["Iâ€™m continuing from the exposure audit and the failed probability filter. The next test will predict net return per unit of risk, then replay its decisions with the measured adverse-cost controls. Iâ€™ll keep the earlier failure and treat these as development tests, not fresh validation.\n"], "text": "Iâ€™m continuing from the exposure audit and the failed probability filter. The next test will predict net return per unit of risk, then replay its decisions with the measured adverse-cost controls. Iâ€™ll keep the earlier failure and treat these as development tests, not fresh validation.\n", "images": [], "source_kind": "visible_chat_event", "index": 230, "text_sha256": "1109d40690d26167a105c8d8da196d34fcc44c9e36a37f472f33ac39545c7889", "section": "conversation"}
{"file": "rollout-2026-10-15T13-43-10-01a13e83-da25-79c2-8413-bcf2766efa8a.jsonl", "line": 10851, "timestamp": "2026-10-16T00:06:23.827Z", "message_id": "msg_0c38f0064b42ade4016ad16a7e633081919ed6e3866f0639e9", "role": "assistant", "phase": "commentary", "parts": ["The new research replay now compares two fixed rules: take a trade when estimated net return is at least 0.10R, or require that estimate to clear an additional error penalty. The penalty is a conservative experiment, not a statistical confidence bound. Both rules wait for 100 closed training outcomes before trading.\n"], "text": "The new research replay now compares two fixed rules: take a trade when estimated net return is at least 0.10R, or require that estimate to clear an additional error penalty. The penalty is a conservative experiment, not a statistical confidence bound. Both rules wait for 100 closed training outcomes before trading.\n", "images": [], "source_kind": "visible_chat_event", "index": 231, "text_sha256": "c8bd26ec64838907de35ba4acd26cab8767a3037d47df1ee9790f95d3dbc6c6e", "section": "conversation"}
{"file": "rollout-2026-10-15T13-43-10-01a13e83-da25-79c2-8413-bcf2766efa8a.jsonl", "line": 10929, "timestamp": "2026-10-16T00:12:23.799Z", "message_id": "msg_0c38f0064b42ade4016ad16be623888191a668c12e79ed928c", "role": "assistant", "phase": "commentary", "parts": ["The payoff engine and replay pass 35 synthetic checks, including delayed learning, actual post-warmup entries, loss-driven skips, and recalculated fills and lot sizes under wider spreads. The market test will cover Aprilâ€“October and retain both policies under all six cost controls, so the 100-label warmup leaves a meaningful period to evaluate.\n"], "text": "The payoff engine and replay pass 35 synthetic checks, including delayed learning, actual post-warmup entries, loss-driven skips, and recalculated fills and lot sizes under wider spreads. The market test will cover Aprilâ€“October and retain both policies under all six cost controls, so the 100-label warmup leaves a meaningful period to evaluate.\n", "images": [], "source_kind": "visible_chat_event", "index": 232, "text_sha256": "59a6d12b882eeccf4b2e1c4c379e78428a8df31ca58bb6a9fb9fc2dc116b0a4d", "section": "conversation"}
