{"file": "rollout-2026-10-15T13-43-10-01a13e83-da25-79c2-8413-bcf2766efa8a.jsonl", "line": 12470, "timestamp": "2026-10-16T01:35:48.434Z", "message_id": "msg_0c38f0064b42ade4016ad17f729cf08191ad66b84e7298b361", "role": "assistant", "phase": "commentary", "parts": ["The Marchâ€“May collection is complete: 3,856,343 original ticks cover all 93,547 native minute timestamps, with no coverage gaps or unresolved cleanup.\n\nThe audit also found a validation bug: moving the same account to another terminal could make previously researched dates appear fresh. I fixed the exposure check, and its new tests pass. Execution still requires the exact terminal identity.\n"], "text": "The Marchâ€“May collection is complete: 3,856,343 original ticks cover all 93,547 native minute timestamps, with no coverage gaps or unresolved cleanup.\n\nThe audit also found a validation bug: moving the same account to another terminal could make previously researched dates appear fresh. I fixed the exposure check, and its new tests pass. Execution still requires the exact terminal identity.\n", "images": [], "source_kind": "visible_chat_event", "index": 259, "text_sha256": "7aa2dab3e4c014eb67d01ce83651dd6140438e255935532bc8240a00a86ce847", "section": "conversation"}
{"file": "rollout-2026-10-15T13-43-10-01a13e83-da25-79c2-8413-bcf2766efa8a.jsonl", "line": 12501, "timestamp": "2026-10-16T01:39:30.054Z", "message_id": "msg_0c38f0064b42ade4016ad1805053308191ad60a4145aa3faa7", "role": "assistant", "phase": "commentary", "parts": ["Iâ€™ll inspect the learning engine already in MarketLink, research relevant GitHub projects, and add whatâ€™s missing to the SMC core. Iâ€™ll focus on learning from trade outcomes without treating a fitted backtest as proof of future profit. Live deployment will stay behind your confirmation.\n"], "text": "Iâ€™ll inspect the learning engine already in MarketLink, research relevant GitHub projects, and add whatâ€™s missing to the SMC core. Iâ€™ll focus on learning from trade outcomes without treating a fitted backtest as proof of future profit. Live deployment will stay behind your confirmation.\n", "images": [], "source_kind": "visible_chat_event", "index": 260, "text_sha256": "5b809a708b7120f014cc3901ebb45f72471e7e0eec6ef2aeaeee67bd69dd3aca", "section": "conversation"}
{"file": "rollout-2026-10-15T13-43-10-01a13e83-da25-79c2-8413-bcf2766efa8a.jsonl", "line": 12560, "timestamp": "2026-10-16T01:41:03.130Z", "message_id": "msg_0c38f0064b42ade4016ad180abf980819185a5b99d2d1eb046", "role": "assistant", "phase": "commentary", "parts": ["MarketLink already has a learner that updates after simulated trades close. The missing piece is showing whether those updates actually improve its predictions.\n\nIâ€™m adding a comparison against a simple forecast that uses only prior closed outcomes. The app will show when the learner performs better or worse, alongside its mistake journal. This follows Riverâ€™s delayed-evaluation approach; FreqAI also warns that continual retraining can overfit. [River](https://github.com/online-ml/river/blob/main/river/evaluate/progressive_validation.py), [FreqAI](https://docs.freqtrade.io/en/stable/freqai-parameter-table/)\n"], "text": "MarketLink already has a learner that updates after simulated trades close. The missing piece is showing whether those updates actually improve its predictions.\n\nIâ€™m adding a comparison against a simple forecast that uses only prior closed outcomes. The app will show when the learner performs better or worse, alongside its mistake journal. This follows Riverâ€™s delayed-evaluation approach; FreqAI also warns that continual retraining can overfit. [River](https://github.com/online-ml/river/blob/main/river/evaluate/progressive_validation.py), [FreqAI](https://docs.freqtrade.io/en/stable/freqai-parameter-table/)\n", "images": [], "source_kind": "visible_chat_event", "index": 261, "text_sha256": "6f5434ed7a31b4d93f8ef834f55cc02991021de765cc7fb3a733e505cc18bfcc", "section": "conversation"}
{"file": "rollout-2026-10-15T13-43-10-01a13e83-da25-79c2-8413-bcf2766efa8a.jsonl", "line": 12654, "timestamp": "2026-10-16T02:13:17.055Z", "message_id": "msg_0c38f0064b42ade4016ad18839d5e88191ad135385ff067879", "role": "assistant", "phase": "commentary", "parts": ["The new learning-quality view is being connected to the app. It will compare predictions on the same closed trades, separate the warmup period, and show whether recent prediction errors are improving.\n\nThe separate EURUSD research dataset also passed an independent source audit: 3,856,343 original ticks, with exact native-minute coverage. No profitability result has been produced from that cohort yet.\n"], "text": "The new learning-quality view is being connected to the app. It will compare predictions on the same closed trades, separate the warmup period, and show whether recent prediction errors are improving.\n\nThe separate EURUSD research dataset also passed an independent source audit: 3,856,343 original ticks, with exact native-minute coverage. No profitability result has been produced from that cohort yet.\n", "images": [], "source_kind": "visible_chat_event", "index": 262, "text_sha256": "8dd9d49dce0d2f9a8d8bd8182184ec394be3f97bbd352604283b304b16773aeb", "section": "conversation"}
{"file": "rollout-2026-10-15T13-43-10-01a13e83-da25-79c2-8413-bcf2766efa8a.jsonl", "line": 12691, "timestamp": "2026-10-16T02:15:54.089Z", "message_id": "msg_0c38f0064b42ade4016ad188d78a58819189e5a81e0ae38e2d", "role": "assistant", "phase": "commentary", "parts": ["The scorecard now keeps prediction improvement separate from trading profit. It shows errors after warmup, errors on the latest 50 scored decisions, and how forecast probabilities compare with observed net wins.\n\nIâ€™m testing the timing rules now, including same-millisecond closes and unavailable outcomes. Then Iâ€™ll package the updated Windows app and run the fixed EURUSD experiment.\n"], "text": "The scorecard now keeps prediction improvement separate from trading profit. It shows errors after warmup, errors on the latest 50 scored decisions, and how forecast probabilities compare with observed net wins.\n\nIâ€™m testing the timing rules now, including same-millisecond closes and unavailable outcomes. Then Iâ€™ll package the updated Windows app and run the fixed EURUSD experiment.\n", "images": [], "source_kind": "visible_chat_event", "index": 263, "text_sha256": "5f438fa99b1c63dd263a8c06c4be6789991c9f65f4043643db3d8742d82aaa34", "section": "conversation"}
