the development gates. No strategy was activated.\n\n[Windows installer](<C:/Users/EHOSANUR RAHMAN ROMI/Downloads/MarketLink-3.5.0-Setup.exe>) Â· [Private GitHub release](https://github.com/EhosanurRahmanRomi/marketlink-mt5-bridge/releases/tag/v3.5.0)\n\n", "images": [], "source_kind": "visible_chat_event", "index": 268, "text_sha256": "4690735851ead6d45f1df69c562b4b6ec72dea5d600f050a60c1822a9440ae0b", "section": "conversation"}
{"file": "rollout-2026-10-15T13-43-10-01a13e83-da25-79c2-8413-bcf2766efa8a.jsonl", "line": 12968, "timestamp": "2026-10-16T02:37:18.032Z", "message_id": "msg_0c38f0064b42ade4016ad18ddb14508191ac0752d499916692", "role": "assistant", "phase": "commentary", "parts": ["The previous turn made concrete progress: MarketLink 3.5 was installed and published, and the new tests ruled out both the current learnerâ€™s prediction advantage and the fixed EURUSD grid hypothesis.\n\nIâ€™ll now investigate a distinct, documented market mechanism. Iâ€™ll check the earlier experiment history first so I donâ€™t repeat a failed idea, and freeze the next test before inspecting its returns.\n"], "text": "The previous turn made concrete progress: MarketLink 3.5 was installed and published, and the new tests ruled out both the current learnerâ€™s prediction advantage and the fixed EURUSD grid hypothesis.\n\nIâ€™ll now investigate a distinct, documented market mechanism. Iâ€™ll check the earlier experiment history first so I donâ€™t repeat a failed idea, and freeze the next test before inspecting its returns.\n", "images": [], "source_kind": "visible_chat_event", "index": 269, "text_sha256": "126824e9a9bb682cd3b6bd25560d3e8fe48ac196b349b6d5ee65a1e568e16b23", "section": "conversation"}
{"file": "rollout-2026-10-15T13-43-10-01a13e83-da25-79c2-8413-bcf2766efa8a.jsonl", "line": 13056, "timestamp": "2026-10-16T02:43:47.322Z", "message_id": "msg_0c38f0064b42ade4016ad18f5f32dc8191ac97e42f14384719", "role": "assistant", "phase": "commentary", "parts": ["The newer research changes the next test. The published paper identifies a replacement European benchmark at **14:00 Frankfurt**, while Londonâ€™s fix remains at **16:00 London**. It also reports that client trading costs can erase the apparent opportunity.\n\nIâ€™ll test two fixed EURUSD windows with a direction-reversed control, proper daylight-saving conversion, holiday exclusions and the same four cost profiles. This will test whether the documented effect is usable with our Exness quotes. [Published paper](https://onlinelibrary.wiley.com/doi/full/10.1111/jofi.13306)\n"], "text": "The newer research changes the next test. The published paper identifies a replacement European benchmark at **14:00 Frankfurt**, while Londonâ€™s fix remains at **16:00 London**. It also reports that client trading costs can erase the apparent opportunity.\n\nIâ€™ll test two fixed EURUSD windows with a direction-reversed control, proper daylight-saving conversion, holiday exclusions and the same four cost profiles. This will test whether the documented effect is usable with our Exness quotes. [Published paper](https://onlinelibrary.wiley.com/doi/full/10.1111/jofi.13306)\n", "images": [], "source_kind": "visible_chat_event", "index": 270, "text_sha256": "d43b75bf4660e90f31fff85ab9768f700a402a7e47864e720e206a4cb6cb55e4", "section": "conversation"}
{"file": "rollout-2026-10-15T13-43-10-01a13e83-da25-79c2-8413-bcf2766efa8a.jsonl", "line": 13207, "timestamp": "2026-10-16T02:53:02.026Z", "message_id": "msg_0c38f0064b42ade4016ad1918b54808191ac94418bfd7d8dbc", "role": "assistant", "phase": "commentary", "parts": ["The new signal tests pass, including the March daylight-saving mismatch and entries on a later quote with the same timestamp.\n\nThe independent review also found an accounting gap: after a quote gap, a late close could be labeled â€œstop lossâ€ and escape a check that only counted late â€œtime exits.â€ Iâ€™m tightening the completeness check for every close reason before the first replay.\n"], "text": "The new signal tests pass, including the March daylight-saving mismatch and entries on a later quote with the same timestamp.\n\nThe independent review also found an accounting gap: after a quote gap, a late close could be labeled â€œstop lossâ€ and escape a check that only counted late â€œtime exits.â€ Iâ€™m tightening the completeness check for every close reason before the first replay.\n", "images": [], "source_kind": "visible_chat_event", "index": 271, "text_sha256": "ae96474fc19c59d38ca0c38626ee4879a792c78d697b498981d326ef9d258de5", "section": "conversation"}
{"file": "rollout-2026-10-15T13-43-10-01a13e83-da25-79c2-8413-bcf2766efa8a.jsonl", "line": 13295, "timestamp": "2026-10-16T02:59:07.978Z", "message_id": "msg_0c38f0064b42ade4016ad192f94bc881918c4c5bd3732ce0c0", "role": "assistant", "phase": "commentary", "parts": ["The fixed experiment is ready. Its independent synthetic check matched **1,126 boundary events and 524 intentions**, with no discrepancies in 11,168 comparisons. The runner also passed its provenance, cost-timing and resource checks.\n\nIâ€™m saving the rules before running the eight accounts: one primary policy and its reversed control under four unchanged cost profiles. No reserved period will be opened.\n"], "text": "The fixed experiment is ready. Its independent synthetic check matched **1,126 boundary events and 524 intentions**, with no discrepancies in 11,168 comparisons. The runner also passed its provenance, cost-timing and resource checks.\n\nIâ€™m saving the rules before running the eight accounts: one primary policy and its reversed control under four unchanged cost profiles. No reserved period will be opened.\n", "images": [], "source_kind": "visible_chat_event", "index": 272, "text_sha256": "09f1cfa06f40d8d44284e8fa8f40426ba71af1ab93ec42121bd7e36fed9fb548", "section": "conversation"}
{"file": "rollout-2026-10-15T13-43-10-01a13e83-da25-79c2-8413-bcf2766efa8a.jsonl", "line": 13333, "timestamp": "2026-10-16T03:04:01.926Z", "message_id": "msg_0c38f0064b42ade4016ad1941e5b148191adefc8ab891e55cf", "role": "assistant", "phase": "commentary", "parts": ["The new fixed-rule experiment finished on 3.86 million retained Exness ticks. It failed: the primary strategy produced PF **0.71** under the standard cost assumptions and **0.62** under stress. Both trading legs lost money overall.\n\nIâ€™m independently checking the replay before recording the result. This also gives the learning engine useful evidence: it must be able to reject a bad strategy, not just keep adjusting it until a backtest looks attractive.\n"], "text": "The new fixed-rule experiment finished on 3.86 million retained Exness ticks. It failed: the primary strategy produced PF **0.71** under the standard cost assumptions and **0.62** under stress. Both trading legs lost money overall.\n\nIâ€™m independently checking the replay before recording the result. This also gives the learning engine useful evidence: it must be able to reject a bad strategy, not just keep adjusting it until a backtest looks attractive.\n", "images": [], "source_kind": "visible_chat_event", "index": 273, "text_sha256": "64f021d494ae2e8e784d0fc596339cf338843bcb9815bc3c113990191a5dfd55", "section": "conversation"}
{"file": "rollout-2026-10-15T13-43-10-01a13e83-da25-79c2-8413-bcf2766efa8a.jsonl", "line": 13385, "timestamp": "2026-10-16T03:05:40.328Z", "message_id": "msg_0c38f0064b42ade4016ad1948067848191bb8e4b47ac2c7f5b", "role": "assistant", "phase": "commentary", "parts": ["All eight accounts failed, including the reversed-direction controls. The source-based primary did worse than the reverse control, and its April and May groups lost money. Iâ€™ve preserved every result; no favorable month or trading leg will be promoted.\n\nThe independent checker will reconstruct decisions and equity from the original quotes. Iâ€™m also reviewing a bounded learning change that could learn when to wait, with delayed labels and costs kept explicit.\n"], "text": "All eight accounts failed, including the reversed-direction controls. The source-based primary did worse than the reverse control, and its April and May groups lost money. Iâ€™ve preserved every result; no favorable month or trading leg will be promoted.\n\nThe independent checker will reconstruct decisions and equity from the original quotes. Iâ€™m also reviewing a bounded learning change that could learn when to wait, with delayed labels and costs kept explicit.\n", "images": [], "source_kind": "visible_chat_event", "index": 274, "text_sha256": "6c406a87c43b932c67e7994f507ece7a874acd2590984c4d8d8014ebc18848d0", "section": "conversation"}
{"file": "rollout-2026-10-15T13-43-10-01a13e83-da25-79c2-8413-bcf2766efa8a.jsonl", "line": 13415, "timestamp": "2026-10-16T03:08:38.378Z", "message_id": "msg_0c38f0064b42ade4016ad19534f92c8191b1bf528e181a03de", "role": "assistant", "phase": "commentary", "parts": ["The parallel review workers stopped with access and usage errors before saving their new audit files. Iâ€™ll continue the check locally using the completed run. The eight-account results and frozen source are intact, and the PC still has about **41 GB free**.\n"], "text": "The parallel review workers stopped with access and usage errors before saving their new audit files. Iâ€™ll continue the check locally using the completed run. The eight-account results and frozen source are intact, and the PC still has about **41 GB free**.\n", "images": [], "source_kind": "visible_chat_event", "index": 275, "text_sha256": "d051b94ff881fae983aa3a691be4e8d4bb42883598b78add6ad269e25bfee8f8", "section": "conversation"}
{"file": "rollout-2026-10-15T13-43-10-01a13e83-da25-79c2-8413-bcf2766efa8a.jsonl", "line": 13445, "timestamp": "2026-10-16T03:12:45.221Z", "message_id": "msg_0c38f0064b42ade4016ad1962b4ae4819199da7e121eb46acc", "role": "assistant", "phase": "commentary", "parts": ["The local audit is written. It rebuilds candles from original Bid quotes, converts the 2026 civil-time schedules independently, and checks entry sizing, costs, exits and drawdown. It treats flat account intervals as constant equity and examines every quote while a position is open.\n\nIâ€™ll run synthetic checks first, then check all eight completed accounts without rerunning or changing the experiment.\n"], "text": "The local audit is written. It rebuilds candles from original Bid quotes, converts the 2026 civil-time schedules independently, and checks entry sizing, costs, exits and drawdown. It treats flat account intervals as constant equity and examines every quote while a position is open.\n\nIâ€™ll run synthetic checks first, then check all eight completed accounts without rerunning or changing the experiment.\n", "images": [], "source_kind": "visible_chat_event", "index": 276, "text_sha256": "2e7c2a3cc395d6c18ddc9cd4f1d1661324c048ca230567c9eb10c373fc77199b", "section": "conversation"}
{"file": "rollout-2026-10-15T13-43-10-01a13e83-da25-79c2-8413-bcf2766efa8a.jsonl", "line": 13496, "timestamp": "2026-10-16T03:15:03.826Z", "message_id": "msg_0c38f0064b42ade4016ad196b602008191b9c8978a93b94e5f", "role": "assistant", "phase": "commentary", "parts": ["The independent audit passed with **zero discrepancies** across **910 trades, 15,080 saved equity points and 38,404 numerical comparisons**. It also recomputed full-quote drawdown and reconstructed the scheduled decisions.\n\nThat confirms the failed results. Iâ€™m saving the complete evidence and rejecting this fixing-based rule from promotion. The profitability goal remains unmet.\n"], "text": "The independent audit passed with **zero discrepancies** across **910 trades, 15,080 saved equity points and 38,404 numerical comparisons**. It also recomputed full-quote drawdown and reconstructed the scheduled decisions.\n\nThat confirms the failed results. Iâ€™m saving the complete evidence and rejecting this fixing-based rule from promotion. The profitability goal remains unmet.\n", "images": [], "source_kind": "visible_chat_event", "index": 277, "text_sha256": "b76114adc84f945027f509941c303bb89013ab465c99d2095a2c894a42f71f21", "section": "conversation"}
{"file": "rollout-2026-10-15T13-43-10-01a13e83-da25-79c2-8413-bcf2766efa8a.jsonl", "line": 13526, "timestamp": "2026-10-16T03:17:33.724Z", "message_id": "msg_0c38f0064b42ade4016ad1974af504819181596471e3c35f86", "role": "assistant", "phase": "commentary", "parts": ["Riverâ€™s current code documents gradual forgetting and model weighting, but those mechanisms still need a trading-specific test. Its online update flow also cannot be used directly for delayed trade labels without preserving the earlier prediction. [River source](https://github.com/online-ml/river/blob/main/river/linear_model/bayesian_lin_reg.py)\n\nIâ€™m narrowing the next learning experiment to one fixed forgetting rate, compared with the existing non-forgetting model and a simple payoff reference. The entry rules, threshold, risk and costs will stay fixed, so the comparison can test whether forgetting adds value.\n"], "text": "Riverâ€™s current code documents gradual forgetting and model weighting, but those mechanisms still need a trading-specific test. Its online update flow also cannot be used directly for delayed trade labels without preserving the earlier prediction. [River source](https://github.com/online-ml/river/blob/main/river/linear_model/bayesian_lin_reg.py)\n\nIâ€™m narrowing the next learning experiment to one fixed forgetting rate, compared with the existing non-forgetting model and a simple payoff reference. The entry rules, threshold, risk and costs will stay fixed, so the comparison can test whether forgetting adds value.\n", "images": [], "source_kind": "visible_chat_event", "index": 278, "text_sha256": "53e2e7041352e12b9d8ab6bb27fddb7a467f7714e66e43968b8f4ffcbcf5a9a9", "section": "conversation"}
