{"file": "rollout-2026-10-15T13-43-10-01a13e83-da25-79c2-8413-bcf2766efa8a.jsonl", "line": 34260, "timestamp": "2026-10-17T14:17:04.913Z", "message_id": "msg_0c38f0064b42ade4016ad3835f8a448191a5c92e44fa79d4a6", "role": "assistant", "phase": "commentary", "parts": ["The installed 4.0.1 app reopened all 128 trials and all seven evaluation accounts successfully. It shows the saved equity chart and the failed requirements, and deployment remains blocked. This gives the future LLM verified results to explain rather than relying on its own recollection of the numbers.\n"], "text": "The installed 4.0.1 app reopened all 128 trials and all seven evaluation accounts successfully. It shows the saved equity chart and the failed requirements, and deployment remains blocked. This gives the future LLM verified results to explain rather than relying on its own recollection of the numbers.\n", "images": [], "source_kind": "visible_chat_event", "index": 567, "text_sha256": "bad61906b842659dae92546518b3cf3c72ef4d7346692fba90777f7ba5acfe0b", "section": "conversation"}
{"file": "rollout-2026-10-15T13-43-10-01a13e83-da25-79c2-8413-bcf2766efa8a.jsonl", "line": 34300, "timestamp": "2026-10-17T14:18:24.273Z", "message_id": "msg_0c38f0064b42ade4016ad383a9f1d48191931837576ecee95f", "role": "assistant", "phase": "final_answer", "parts": ["Yesâ€”a **local AI coordinator** is the right direction for organizing the app.\n\nIt should provide:\n\n- **Chat:** explain strategies, results, and failures.\n- **Commands:** start supported backtests, monitor progress, and stop jobs.\n- **Research memory:** retrieve documented findings and previous experiments.\n\nThe application will validate calculations and commands. Training alone cannot guarantee profitable trading.\n\nIâ€™ve saved the [LLM integration design](<C:/Users/EHOSANUR RAHMAN ROMI/Desktop/codex/mt5-desktop-bridge/docs/LOCAL-LLM-COORDINATOR-DESIGN-2026.md>). The new coordinator is **planned, not yet installed or trained**, keeping ICT as the priority.\n\n**Current delivery:** MarketLink 4.0.1 is installed. I verified the ICT chart, saved equity, trade ledger, and all seven evaluations.\n\n[Windows installer](<C:/Users/EHOSANUR RAHMAN ROMI/Desktop/codex/mt5-desktop-bridge/release/MarketLink-Setup-4.0.1-local.exe>) Â· [Verified private GitHub release](https://github.com/EhosanurRahmanRomi/marketlink-mt5-bridge/releases/tag/v4.0.1-ict-preview.1)\n\nThe ICT strategy remains unqualified: full-window PF **2.19 on only 10 trades**, with final-segment PF **0.53**. Deployment remains blocked.\n\n"], "text": "Yesâ€”a **local AI coordinator** is the right direction for organizing the app.\n\nIt should provide:\n\n- **Chat:** explain strategies, results, and failures.\n- **Commands:** start supported backtests, monitor progress, and stop jobs.\n- **Research memory:** retrieve documented findings and previous experiments.\n\nThe application will validate calculations and commands. Training alone cannot guarantee profitable trading.\n\nIâ€™ve saved the [LLM integration design](<C:/Users/EHOSANUR RAHMAN ROMI/Desktop/codex/mt5-desktop-bridge/docs/LOCAL-LLM-COORDINATOR-DESIGN-2026.md>). The new coordinator is **planned, not yet installed or trained**, keeping ICT as the priority.\n\n**Current delivery:** MarketLink 4.0.1 is installed. I verified the ICT chart, saved equity, trade ledger, and all seven evaluations.\n\n[Windows installer](<C:/Users/EHOSANUR RAHMAN ROMI/Desktop/codex/mt5-desktop-bridge/release/MarketLink-Setup-4.0.1-local.exe>) Â· [Verified private GitHub release](https://github.com/EhosanurRahmanRomi/marketlink-mt5-bridge/releases/tag/v4.0.1-ict-preview.1)\n\nThe ICT strategy remains unqualified: full-window PF **2.19 on only 10 trades**, with final-segment PF **0.53**. Deployment remains blocked.\n\n", "images": [], "source_kind": "visible_chat_event", "index": 568, "text_sha256": "e91711bd5bbf0041456bf85a5c5145a025d7524e263a26cd43937dd5ad4f0ad8", "section": "conversation"}
{"file": "rollout-2026-10-15T13-43-10-01a13e83-da25-79c2-8413-bcf2766efa8a.jsonl", "line": 34310, "timestamp": "2026-10-17T14:18:42.654Z", "message_id": "msg_0c38f0064b42ade4016ad383c10ac48191a1aaea90b0ecbe79", "role": "assistant", "phase": "commentary", "parts": ["The last turn made concrete progress: the installed ICT workspace passed the saved-study checks, and both local downloads and the private GitHub release were verified. Iâ€™m returning to the strategy core now. The next task is to specify and test the separate hourly-reversal/inversion model from its original teaching, starting with its opportunity count before another optimization run.\n"], "text": "The last turn made concrete progress: the installed ICT workspace passed the saved-study checks, and both local downloads and the private GitHub release were verified. Iâ€™m returning to the strategy core now. The next task is to specify and test the separate hourly-reversal/inversion model from its original teaching, starting with its opportunity count before another optimization run.\n", "images": [], "source_kind": "visible_chat_event", "index": 569, "text_sha256": "5d02e7d068943b3e70b0fb3e7c6da70185598feca75ea87fbf466088d08c9499", "section": "conversation"}
{"file": "rollout-2026-10-15T13-43-10-01a13e83-da25-79c2-8413-bcf2766efa8a.jsonl", "line": 34408, "timestamp": "2026-10-17T14:23:01.437Z", "message_id": "msg_0c38f0064b42ade4016ad384b50d7881918152a505ed79a4fd", "role": "assistant", "phase": "commentary", "parts": ["The additional source review found an important timing distinction: TTrades describes lower-timeframe CISD confirmation **inside the higher-timeframe reversal candle**. Our earlier draft required a new confirmation after that candle closed. Iâ€™m keeping the old draft intact and building a separately versioned model that preserves the confirmation already formed inside the hour. The exact zone formula remains our declared adaptation because the public material does not fully define T-Spot. [Source](https://ttrades.com/how-change-in-the-state-of-delivery-cisd-confirms-swing-points/)\n"], "text": "The additional source review found an important timing distinction: TTrades describes lower-timeframe CISD confirmation **inside the higher-timeframe reversal candle**. Our earlier draft required a new confirmation after that candle closed. Iâ€™m keeping the old draft intact and building a separately versioned model that preserves the confirmation already formed inside the hour. The exact zone formula remains our declared adaptation because the public material does not fully define T-Spot. [Source](https://ttrades.com/how-change-in-the-state-of-delivery-cisd-confirms-swing-points/)\n", "images": [], "source_kind": "visible_chat_event", "index": 570, "text_sha256": "72176793ef3c1a38933bcd0c82310d9b4a014c3e974cbee9f767287090cda0ee", "section": "conversation"}
