{"file": "rollout-2026-10-15T13-43-10-01a13e83-da25-79c2-8413-bcf2766efa8a.jsonl", "line": 40668, "timestamp": "2026-10-17T22:37:26.747Z", "message_id": "msg_008a0b1dd3e1111d016ad3f8a5907881918db79048e1bfeeaf", "role": "assistant", "phase": "commentary", "parts": ["The MT5 export has reached roughly 65%â€”about 12.6 million original quotes copied. The existing 41 search checks pass. New tests are now checking concurrent execution, identical serial/parallel results, Stop handling, and saved-run loading."], "text": "The MT5 export has reached roughly 65%â€”about 12.6 million original quotes copied. The existing 41 search checks pass. New tests are now checking concurrent execution, identical serial/parallel results, Stop handling, and saved-run loading.", "images": [], "source_kind": "visible_chat_event", "index": 687, "text_sha256": "35125d57a23f7ae32c5633bb4a9fa2920b354f208897a4b488ee134be0365a2a", "section": "conversation"}
{"file": "rollout-2026-10-15T13-43-10-01a13e83-da25-79c2-8413-bcf2766efa8a.jsonl", "line": 40700, "timestamp": "2026-10-17T22:38:18.302Z", "message_id": "msg_008a0b1dd3e1111d016ad3f8d96f6081918b1d86a99a124901", "role": "assistant", "phase": "commentary", "parts": ["The first parallel test run confirms that accounts overlap, stay within the worker limit, and preserve original tick order with separate file readers. Stop and worker-failure checks also pass. Iâ€™m investigating a result-comparison mismatch before packaging the update."], "text": "The first parallel test run confirms that accounts overlap, stay within the worker limit, and preserve original tick order with separate file readers. Stop and worker-failure checks also pass. Iâ€™m investigating a result-comparison mismatch before packaging the update.", "images": [], "source_kind": "visible_chat_event", "index": 688, "text_sha256": "60ad33440bd5c8a67b3a5c0174ca00b0d38038cdebb125dc12e5cdb6f7b8f946", "section": "conversation"}
{"file": "rollout-2026-10-15T13-43-10-01a13e83-da25-79c2-8413-bcf2766efa8a.jsonl", "line": 40719, "timestamp": "2026-10-17T22:39:17.575Z", "message_id": "01a14c04-fc24-7431-91e4-31fc5ba45667", "role": "user", "phase": null, "parts": ["can you give a brif summery that what about the progess and how the ict core works?\n"], "text": "can you give a brif summery that what about the progess and how the ict core works?\n", "images": [], "source_kind": "visible_chat_event", "index": 689, "text_sha256": "7c4076fd2f2c02fc4168f8995cc5057454b4ec7f8db03d7cb62c705dbb4642ff", "section": "conversation"}
{"file": "rollout-2026-10-15T13-43-10-01a13e83-da25-79c2-8413-bcf2766efa8a.jsonl", "line": 40729, "timestamp": "2026-10-17T22:39:35.836Z", "message_id": "msg_008a0b1dd3e1111d016ad3f92189388191b6b434a97fd4579f", "role": "assistant", "phase": "commentary", "parts": ["The ICT foundation is built: its own UI, original MT5 tick replay, parameter search, charts, trade ledger, saved results, and Stop controls. The all-core CPU update is being tested. **No strategy has yet passed the full profitability requirements.**\n\nThe default ICT core works like this:\n\n1. **Direction:** confirmed M15 swing structure identifies an upward or downward bias.\n2. **Setup:** during selected London/New York windows, it looks for a strong move that creates a fair value gap.\n3. **Entry:** it waits for price to retrace into that gap, aligned with the bias.\n4. **Filters:** it skips expired setups, broken structure, and trades without enough room to an untouched liquidity target.\n5. **Risk:** it uses a structure-based stop, configured reward/risk, and 0.25% risk per trade. Backtests include recorded Bid/Ask spread, fees, and adverse slippage.\n\nOnly information available at that moment can trigger a decision. Optimization selects parameters on training data, freezes them, then tests later periods and higher costs. Longer testing can find better candidates, but improvement and PF 2 are not guaranteed."], "text": "The ICT foundation is built: its own UI, original MT5 tick replay, parameter search, charts, trade ledger, saved results, and Stop controls. The all-core CPU update is being tested. **No strategy has yet passed the full profitability requirements.**\n\nThe default ICT core works like this:\n\n1. **Direction:** confirmed M15 swing structure identifies an upward or downward bias.\n2. **Setup:** during selected London/New York windows, it looks for a strong move that creates a fair value gap.\n3. **Entry:** it waits for price to retrace into that gap, aligned with the bias.\n4. **Filters:** it skips expired setups, broken structure, and trades without enough room to an untouched liquidity target.\n5. **Risk:** it uses a structure-based stop, configured reward/risk, and 0.25% risk per trade. Backtests include recorded Bid/Ask spread, fees, and adverse slippage.\n\nOnly information available at that moment can trigger a decision. Optimization selects parameters on training data, freezes them, then tests later periods and higher costs. Longer testing can find better candidates, but improvement and PF 2 are not guaranteed.", "images": [], "source_kind": "visible_chat_event", "index": 690, "text_sha256": "931c45471036862e99cf226b7eaeee84c0b3e0aa5135e7fd38c6f5ce60dcded9", "section": "conversation"}
