{"file": "rollout-2026-10-15T13-43-10-01a13e83-da25-79c2-8413-bcf2766efa8a.jsonl", "line": 18714, "timestamp": "2026-10-16T11:27:17.751Z", "message_id": "msg_0c38f0064b42ade4016ad20a0fdffc8191abb9373aae72f499", "role": "assistant", "phase": "final_answer", "parts": ["I redesigned and saved the [full project goal](</C:/Users/EHOSANUR RAHMAN ROMI/Desktop/codex/mt5-desktop-bridge/docs/MARKETLINK-PROJECT-GOAL-2026.md>) and pushed it to your private GitHub repository.\n\n**First target:** one reproducible XAUUSDm strategy over the latest 90 completed days of 2026, seeking **PF â‰¥1.7, preferably â‰¥2**, after spread, fees and modeled slippageâ€”with sufficient trades and controlled drawdown.\n\nThe development order is:\n\n1. Finish and independently audit the current study.\n2. Improve acquisition, saved results, Stop behavior and UI reliability.\n3. Complete the new linked SMC engine with structural stops and targets.\n4. Test a declared comparison, freeze one training winner, then evaluate later periods.\n5. Verify in native MT5 and demo trading.\n6. Add useful self-learning, other strategies and markets.\n\nThe brief defines acceptance criteria, resource limits and failure handling. **Profitability remains unproven; the current study continues unchanged.**\n\n<oai-mem-citation>\n<citation_entries>\nMEMORY.md:185-185|note=[kept implementation checks separate from native profitability proof]\n</citation_entries>\n<rollout_ids>\n01a0dd88-38fa-7712-8056-cd0d27684bf4\n</rollout_ids>\n</oai-mem-citation>"], "text": "I redesigned and saved the [full project goal](</C:/Users/EHOSANUR RAHMAN ROMI/Desktop/codex/mt5-desktop-bridge/docs/MARKETLINK-PROJECT-GOAL-2026.md>) and pushed it to your private GitHub repository.\n\n**First target:** one reproducible XAUUSDm strategy over the latest 90 completed days of 2026, seeking **PF â‰¥1.7, preferably â‰¥2**, after spread, fees and modeled slippageâ€”with sufficient trades and controlled drawdown.\n\nThe development order is:\n\n1. Finish and independently audit the current study.\n2. Improve acquisition, saved results, Stop behavior and UI reliability.\n3. Complete the new linked SMC engine with structural stops and targets.\n4. Test a declared comparison, freeze one training winner, then evaluate later periods.\n5. Verify in native MT5 and demo trading.\n6. Add useful self-learning, other strategies and markets.\n\nThe brief defines acceptance criteria, resource limits and failure handling. **Profitability remains unproven; the current study continues unchanged.**\n\n<oai-mem-citation>\n<citation_entries>\nMEMORY.md:185-185|note=[kept implementation checks separate from native profitability proof]\n</citation_entries>\n<rollout_ids>\n01a0dd88-38fa-7712-8056-cd0d27684bf4\n</rollout_ids>\n</oai-mem-citation>", "images": [], "source_kind": "original_assistant_output", "index": 20, "text_sha256": "e3bea42c24f593ee14d6f1cbc15f39af6973ac0b757d9e3ec1d093b9f1e4c368", "section": "original_answer_variant"}
{"file": "rollout-2026-10-15T13-43-10-01a13e83-da25-79c2-8413-bcf2766efa8a.jsonl", "line": 21242, "timestamp": "2026-10-16T17:50:22.010Z", "message_id": "msg_0c38f0064b42ade4016ad263d2e1b48191922464453868b916", "role": "assistant", "phase": "final_answer", "parts": ["**The app works, but we have not found a qualifying profitable strategy. Iâ€™ve paused work for this handoff.**\n\n- **App:** MarketLink **3.8.0 is installed**. The MT5 demo connection, live chart and saved partial-result viewer have been verified. Its build passed **1,200 software checks**.\n- **90-day SMC study:** 239 trades, **PF 0.728**, net **âˆ’$840.31** under the declared costs. Rejected.\n- **Linked SMC study:** all 32 training configurations and seven evaluations produced **zero trades**. Rejected. Both studiesâ€™ saved-evidence audits found no discrepancies within their stated scopes.\n- **Loading improvement:** the staged loader reopened the actual completed study in **8m35s**, versus **21m45s** previously. It is **not installed yet**.\n\n**Best finding:** the linked SMC setup chain fails before entry confirmation. Changing reward/risk values alone cannot fix its zero signals. We need to improve opportunity generation and test whether learning adds value.\n\nThe [redesigned goal](</C:/Users/EHOSANUR RAHMAN ROMI/Desktop/codex/mt5-desktop-bridge/docs/MARKETLINK-PROJECT-GOAL-2026.md>) is saved locally. Latest changes remain uncommitted.\n\n**Next step:** finish reviewing the independent opportunity-learning design, implement its delayed feedback and comparison models, then run a bounded 90-day experiment. **PF â‰¥1.7 remains mandatory; PF â‰¥2 preferred.** No strategy has been activated.\n\n<oai-mem-citation>\n<citation_entries>\nMEMORY.md:185-185|note=[kept implementation checks separate from native profitability proof]\n</citation_entries>\n<rollout_ids>\n01a0dd88-38fa-7712-8056-cd0d27684bf4\n</rollout_ids>\n</oai-mem-citation>"], "text": "**The app works, but we have not found a qualifying profitable strategy. Iâ€™ve paused work for this handoff.**\n\n- **App:** MarketLink **3.8.0 is installed**. The MT5 demo connection, live chart and saved partial-result viewer have been verified. Its build passed **1,200 software checks**.\n- **90-day SMC study:** 239 trades, **PF 0.728**, net **âˆ’$840.31** under the declared costs. Rejected.\n- **Linked SMC study:** all 32 training configurations and seven evaluations produced **zero trades**. Rejected. Both studiesâ€™ saved-evidence audits found no discrepancies within their stated scopes.\n- **Loading improvement:** the staged loader reopened the actual completed study in **8m35s**, versus **21m45s** previously. It is **not installed yet**.\n\n**Best finding:** the linked SMC setup chain fails before entry confirmation. Changing reward/risk values alone cannot fix its zero signals. We need to improve opportunity generation and test whether learning adds value.\n\nThe [redesigned goal](</C:/Users/EHOSANUR RAHMAN ROMI/Desktop/codex/mt5-desktop-bridge/docs/MARKETLINK-PROJECT-GOAL-2026.md>) is saved locally. Latest changes remain uncommitted.\n\n**Next step:** finish reviewing the independent opportunity-learning design, implement its delayed feedback and comparison models, then run a bounded 90-day experiment. **PF â‰¥1.7 remains mandatory; PF â‰¥2 preferred.** No strategy has been activated.\n\n<oai-mem-citation>\n<citation_entries>\nMEMORY.md:185-185|note=[kept implementation checks separate from native profitability proof]\n</citation_entries>\n<rollout_ids>\n01a0dd88-38fa-7712-8056-cd0d27684bf4\n</rollout_ids>\n</oai-mem-citation>", "images": [], "source_kind": "original_assistant_output", "index": 21, "text_sha256": "319afc8c3a57548706effbf49a178b6488fb0641292523e70c928bd6d050a077", "section": "original_answer_variant"}
