ess you explicitly change them.\n\nThe next bounded task should be **M0: map the actual current application against this roadmap**, identifying what we can reuse, what is tested and what remains incomplete. That will preserve the work already built and give us one clear next milestone.\n\n<oai-mem-citation>\n<citation_entries>\nMEMORY.md:29-30|note=[preserved private ownership and local broker data boundaries]\n</citation_entries>\n<rollout_ids>\n01a13190-04da-7773-af76-0aa89a528609\n</rollout_ids>\n</oai-mem-citation>"], "text": "Iâ€™ve read **both files fully**, including every milestone, acceptance check and the master planâ€™s 53-source register.\n\n- [Master research and execution plan](<C:/Users/EHOSANUR RAHMAN ROMI/Downloads/CODEX_TRADING_APP_MASTER_PLAN.md>)\n- [Six-foundation task pack](<C:/Users/EHOSANUR RAHMAN ROMI/Downloads/MarketLink_6_Foundations_Codex_Plan.md>)\n\nThey provide a useful proposed roadmap. The master document supplies the detailed specification; the shorter file supplies practical task templates. Their embedded prompts are **future task templates**, so I havenâ€™t started executing them from this reading request.\n\nThe proposed organization preserves your original ideas:\n\n| Foundation | Main scope |\n|---|---|\n| F1 | SMC, ICT, liquidity sweeps, FVG and supply/demand |\n| F2 | Trend and momentum, including EMA |\n| F3 | Volume profile, auction/value and VWAP |\n| F4 | Volatility expansion and breakouts |\n| F5 | Statistical mean reversion |\n| F6 | Order flow, when suitable data exists |\n\nSMC and ICT can retain separate screens, while related signals from one setup count as one foundation vote.\n\nThe development sequence is clear: **audit existing work â†’ shared data/contracts â†’ verified simulator â†’ research specifications â†’ one foundation at a time â†’ walk-forward evaluation â†’ combinations â†’ dashboard â†’ shadow/demo â†’ local LLM â†’ release hardening.** Each milestone gets tested and reviewed before the next begins.\n\nA few differences need reconciliation during the audit: F3/F5 implementation order, F3â€™s first setup, 90 days versus three calendar months, forward-window duration, and proposed PF thresholds. **Your existing PF target of 2.0 and minimum 1.7 remain unchanged** unless you explicitly change them.\n\nThe next bounded task should be **M0: map the actual current application against this roadmap**, identifying what we can reuse, what is tested and what remains incomplete. That will preserve the work already built and give us one clear next milestone.\n\n<oai-mem-citation>\n<citation_entries>\nMEMORY.md:29-30|note=[preserved private ownership and local broker data boundaries]\n</citation_entries>\n<rollout_ids>\n01a13190-04da-7773-af76-0aa89a528609\n</rollout_ids>\n</oai-mem-citation>", "images": [], "source_kind": "original_assistant_output", "index": 46, "text_sha256": "2c9fbc704913644c1c320b6b0b1e6a82c0d766c9cce6134457bd8b277610f799", "section": "original_answer_variant"}
